% ============================================================
% fundstyle.sty
% Style for the ChemicalQDevice daily funding action packets deposited in
% funding/auto-fund.  Repository v4.8.0.
%
% THIS COPY IS DAY 5, 08Sep26, "The Execution Record".  Its accent is Ember Rust
% #8A4B2A with #B57A55 and #EFE1D8 as its two lighter shades.  The five daily
% copies of this file differ ONLY in the six hex values of the palette block
% below; every line beneath that block is identical across the five, so a
% correction made once can be applied five times without reading five files.
%
% WHAT THIS STYLE IS.  It adapts capstyle.sty from
% funding/capitalization-plan/final-capital and keeps that work's five TikZ
% diagram vocabularies, one per machine-readable diagram platform:
%
%   1) mermaid-type            (mm* styles)   flowchart / sequence / state / gantt
%   2) plantuml-type           (uml* styles)  use case / state with guards / activity
%   3) d2-type                 (d2* styles)   containers, grids, sql tables, layers
%   4) diagrams (python)-type  (dg* styles)   clustered infrastructure with glyphs
%   5) graphviz-type           (gv* styles)   dot records, clusters, fault trees
%
% WHAT IS NEW HERE.  Five things, and nothing else.
%
%   a) THE SPACING INVARIANT IS -0.60cm.  appfig and apptable each close with a
%      RIGID \vskip 24.5pt, and \figcaption and \tabcap each open with
%      \nointerlineskip, so the source order
%          \end{appfig}  \vspace{-0.60cm}  \figcaption{...}
%      leaves exactly 24.5pt - 0.60cm = 7.44pt from the last rule to the first
%      caption line, for every figure and every table in every packet, floating
%      or inline, whatever precedes or follows it on the page.  A packet's
%      caption whitespace signature is therefore identical everywhere.
%
%   b) CAPTIONS ARE TWO LINES.  \figcaption and \tabcap set a centered italic
%      block broken by hand onto exactly two lines of near-equal width, each
%      opening with its own number, "Figure N. " or "Table N. ".  The two lines
%      of one caption are held within a small character spread of each other.
%
%   c) A NEW COVER.  \fundmast is a solid accent header block with reversed-out
%      type over a white ruled panel, and \funddeck is a three-cell decision
%      strip.  It is neither the RFA-RM-27-001-v2 centered form-field theme nor
%      the parent work's ruled panel over a three-cell money ledger: a daily
%      action packet leads with what is being decided, so the decision is the
%      first thing on the page and the money is the third.
%
%   d) THE PALETTE IS PER-DAY.  Every color in this file is declared in the one
%      palette block below.  A packet is re-themed by changing the six accent
%      hex values in that block and nothing else; the structural code beneath it
%      is identical across the five packets, so a correction made once applies
%      five times.  No fill token is near-black: black survives as a stroke
%      color and as text only.
%
%   e) NO STICK FIGURES.  The parent style shipped a \umlactor macro that drew a
%      circle-and-limbs actor.  It is deleted rather than left unused, because a
%      basic human stick figure reads as unprofessional in a document a funder
%      will open.  Where the parent would have drawn an actor, this style uses a
%      labeled umlbox or a dgtile carrying a vector pictogram.
%
% SENIOR-AUTHOR FORMATTING.  RaggedRight body with even interword spacing and no
% right-margin overflow; maximal widow, orphan and broken penalties so no single
% line is stranded and no paragraph ends in a one-word or two-word line; long
% URLs break on any character; single hyphens only, no em dash and no double
% dash; the section symbol for every codified reference.  No raster image is
% used or produced anywhere.
%
% COMPILE.  Overleaf, pdfLaTeX:
%   pdflatex main -> bibtex main -> pdflatex main -> pdflatex main
% ============================================================
\NeedsTeXFormat{LaTeX2e}
\ProvidesPackage{fundstyle}[2026/09/02 v4.8.0 ChemicalQDevice daily funding packet style]

